    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced between bullish long-term fundamentals and bearish short-term technicals. The bull case rests on strong fundamentals ($84.95B operating cash flow, $527.85B assets, $201.88B equity) and a textbook bullish moving average stack with price 7.4% above the 50-day and 23.8% above the 200-day SMA. However, the bear's near-term concerns are equally valid: the 5-day return is -1.61%, the MACD histogram has been negative for ~two weeks, the stock was rejected at the upper Bollinger Band ($178.79 intraday high vs. $179.65 band, closing at $175.35), and relative volume at 0.86 is below average. Given the extended position and deteriorating short-term momentum, chasing at $175.35 is not prudent. A HOLD respects the intact long-term trend while avoiding a poor entry point. I would maintain existing positions with a stop/review near the 20-day SMA at $173.24, and only add on either a confirmed breakout above $179.65 on above-average volume or a pullback into the $163-167 support zone.\n\n**Entry Price**: 175.35\n\n**Stop Loss**: 173.24\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain current position; if adding on breakout above $179.65 or pullback to $163-167, size at roughly half of full target allocation\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
